    "ls|LS16_S12_U_128": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \nDEPARTMENT OF FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 128  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 25TH   JULY, 2017 \n \nPUBLIC DISTRIBUTION SYSTEM \n \n*128.  SHRI GEORGE BAKER: \nPROF. RICHARD HAY: \n \nWill the Minister of CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND PUBLIC \nDISTRIBUTION miHkksDrk ekeys] [kk| vkSj lkoZtfud forj.k ea=h   be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the salient features of the Public Distribution System;  \n \n(b)  the details of the funds sanctioned,  allocated and utilised under this \nsystem across the country during the last three years and the current year, \nState/UT-wise;  \n \n(c)  the number of Fair Price Shops  opened across the country to \ndistribute essential commodities to the poor people, State/UT-wise; \n \n(d)  the number of persons/families benefited from this system across the \ncountry during the said period, State/UT  wise along with the rates of items \nbeing provided under the System; and \n \n(e)  whether the Government is planning to increase the rates of the \nitems being provided under this system, if so, the details  thereof along with \nthe reasons therefor and the time by which it is likely to be increased? \n \n \nA N S W E R \nMINISTER OF CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n(SHRI RAMVILAS PASWAN) \n \n \n(a) to (e):  A statement is laid on the table of the House \n \n****  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) to (e) OF THE STARRED \nQUESTION NUMBER *128 DUE FOR ANSWER ON 25.07.2017 IN THE LOK \nSABHA. \n (a):   Salient features of the Public Distribution System are as follows:- \n(i)  Subsidized foodgrains are distributed to beneficiaries/families \nunder the provisions of    National Food Security Act (NFSA), 2013 \nwhich was notified on 10.9.2013 and has since been adopted by all \nStates/UTs. \n(ii)  The Act provides for coverage of upto 75% of rural population and \nupto 50% of urban population at the all India level. \n(iii)  The Priority Households are entitled to receive 5 Kg of foodgrains \nper person per month at the rate of Rs. 3/2/1 for \nrice/wheat/coarsegrains.  The families covered under the category \nof Antodaya Anna Yojana (AAY) receive 35 kg of foodgrains per \nmonth at the same rate.   \n(iv)  NFSA is operated under the joint responsibility of Central and State \nGovernments.  Central Government is res ponsible for procurement, \nallocation and transportation of foodgrains upto to the designated \ndepots of the Food Corporation of India (FCI).  The operational \nresponsibilities for allocation of foodgrains within the States/UTs, \ndistribution of foodgrains to eligible beneficiaries under TPDS and \nsupervision over and monitoring and functioning of the Fair Price \nShops etc. rest with the State/UT Government. \n \n (b):  Under Public Distribution System(PDS), foodgrains are allocated as \nper  the provisions of NFSA. Im plementation of NFSA in different States/UTs \nstarted at different dates. Till any State/UT joined the NFSA, allocation of the \nfoodgrains under erstwhile TPDS was continued to them. Allocation of \nfoodgrains to States/UTs under erstwhile TPDS/NFSA, is at subsidized prices \nand the entire subsidy burden is borne by the Central government. A \nStatement indicating State- wise allocation and offtake of foodgrains is at \nAnnexure-I and year -wise detail of the expenditure on food subsidy is at \nAnnexure –II. \n(c):   5,27,349 Fairs Price Shops are operational as on 30.6.2017.  A \nstatement indicating State- wise number of Fair Price Shops is at Annexure-\nIII. \n \n(d): As stated above, Implementation of NFSA in different States/UTs \nstarted at different dates. Total number of beneficiaries presently covered \nunder NFSA is about 80.55 crore, State/UT -wise detail of which is at \nAnnexure-IV. Subsidised rates for foodgrains are as mentioned in Para 1(iii). \n \n(e):  The current issue prices shall continue upto June, 2018.  \n****  \n \n \n\n \nANNEXURE-I \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART ( b) OF THE STARRED \nQUESTION NUMBER *128 DUE FOR ANSWER ON 25.07.2017 IN THE LOK \nSABHA. \n \nAllocation & Offtake of Rice+Wheat underTPDS/ NFSA during 2014-15 to 2017-18 \n(in thousand tonnes) \n \n2014-15 2015-16 2016-17 2017-18 \nupto 30.6.2017 \nS.No State/UT Allocation Offtake Allocation Offtake Allocation Offtake Allocation Offtake \n1 \nआंध प्र द Andhra \nPradesh 2629.793 1587.263 2110.254 2069.543 1871.844 1845.789 467.961 480.896 \n2 \nअरुणाच प्र द \nArunachal Pradesh  101.556 96.646 101.556 101.417 88.992 87.048 22.248 23.969 \n3 असम Assam 1890.094 1840.293 1811.924 1654.279 1686.864 1564.721 423.783 457.291 \n4 �बहणर Bihar  4914.900 3938.148 5241.275 5025.021 5493.864 5246.761 1373.466 1504.930 \n5 छत्तससग Chhatisgarh 1337.466 1329.701 1384.056 1384.056 1384.056 1268.718 346.014 346.014 \n6 �्लचल Delhi 356.693 360.925 424.500 425.886 450.590 442.669 112.716 121.090 \n7 सोवण Goa 63.148 57.239 61.692 64.072 59.016 58.115 14.751 14.673 \n8 सुजरण् Gujarat 2087.795 1885.738 2085.108 2016.456 2179.372 2174.734 582.382 569.595 \n9 ह�रयणुण Haryana  795.000 801.000 795.000 780.211 795.000 751.000 198.750 227.029 \n10 \n�हमणाच प्र द Himachal \nPradesh 507.996 498.365 507.996 511.970 508.024 504.691 127.008 124.443 \n11 \nजममम - कशमतर Jammu \n& Kashmir 756.804 666.045 755.852 747.628 751.080 748.255 187.770 184.800 \n12 झणरखण् Jharkhand  1359.442 958.781 1460.148 1096.211 1675.879 1637.775 434.880 429.666 \n13 कनणर्क Karnataka  2542.657 2313.096 2608.836 2238.332 2608.836 2222.899 652.209 842.223 \n14 कररच Kerala 1474.349 1441.726 1472.688 1465.038 1370.810 1368.118 356.262 372.066 \n15 \nमधय प्र द Madhya \nPradesh 3194.247 2911.381 3390.015 3182.270 3472.032 3163.436 868.008 800.868 \n16 महणरणष् Maharashtra  4527.492 4045.779 4605.192 4324.368 4605.192 4238.045 1151.298 1027.098 \n17 म�ुपुर Manipur 171.379 172.281 170.952 170.953 141.564 133.058 35.627 