    "ls|LS16_S12_U_144": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP\n \n \nLOK\n \nSABHA\n \n \nSTARRED\n \nQUESTION NO.\n*144\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON \n26 JULY\n, 2017\n \n \nNEW \nINDUSTRIAL TRAINING \nINSTITUTES \n \n \n \n*144\n.\nSHRI JUGAL KISHORE\n:\n \n \nWill the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND \nENTREPRENEURSHIP be pleased to \nState:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether there is a proposal to setup new Industrial Training Institutes (ITIs)\n \nin the State \nof Jammu and Kashmir (J & K) for imparting industrial training to more and more youth and \ndeveloping their skill;\n \n \n(b)  \n \nif so, the details thereof;\n \n \n(c) \n \nwhether there is a need for improving the quality of training being provided by the ITIs \nfunctioning   at present in the country; and\n \n \n(d)  \n \nif so, the details thereof and the steps taken/being taken in this regard?\n \n \nANSW\nER\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) IN \n \nTHE MINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP\n \n(SHRI RAJIV PRATAP RUDY)\n \n \n(a) to (\nd\n) \n \nA statement is laid on the table of the House.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) TO (\nd\n) OF \nLOK\n \nSABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. *\n144\n \nRAISED BY HON’BLE M.P \nSHRI JUGAL KISHORE \nREGARDING \n‘\nNEW INDUSTRIAL TRAINING INSTITUTES\n’ \nFOR REPLY ON 2\n6.0\n7\n.2017.\n \n \n(a) & (b) \n \nNo Madam\n, \nVocational Training is a concurrent subject under the Constitution \nwherein the Central \nGovernment is entrusted with the responsibility of formulation of policy, \nlaying down training standards, norms, whereas implementation and day to day \nadministration, rests with the resp\nective State \nGovernment/Union Territory\n \nconcerned\n/\nprivate\n \nentities\n.\n \n \n(c) & (d) \n \nDirectorate General of Training under Ministry of Skill D\nevelopment and \nEntrepreneurship \nas \nbeen making continuous efforts \nto improve the quality of training being \noffered by the ITIs functioning in the country\n,\n \nwhich \ninclude:\n \n \ni\n.\n \nPrescribing new A\nffiliation Norms for ITIs\n \nfor quality training\n.\n \nii\n.\n \nRegular inspection of ITIs and de\n-\naffiliation of ITIs \nto weed out \nITIs not confo\nrming\n \nto\n \nthe NCVT norms & standards\n.\n \niii\n.\n \nISO 29990 Certification of ITIs\n \nto raise the overall quality and standards\n.\n \niv\n.\n \nGrading of ITIs\n \nto evaluate \ntheir \nperformance\n.\n \nv\n.\n \nIntroduction of new trades & removal of obsolete trades\n \nfor industry relevance\n.\n \nvi\n.\n \nRegular up\n-\ngradation of training content of ITI \ncurriculum\n \nas per industrial \nrequirement\n \nvii\n.\n \n \nAligning the course of CTS to National Skills Qualific\nation Framework (NQSF) \n \nviii\n.\n \n \nImplementation of ‘Dual System of Training’ in ITIs\n \nleading to better ITI \n–\n \nIndustry \nlinkage\n.\n \nix\n.\n \nTraining and re\n-\ntraining of \nITI Instructors\n.\n \nx\n.\n \nUp gradation of infrastructure of ITIs through following centrally funded schemes:\n \n \na\n)\n \nWorld \nBank assisted Vocational Training Improvement Project (VTIP)/Skills \nStrengthening for Industrial Value Enhancement (STRIVE).\n \nb\n)\n \nUp\n-\ngradation of 1396 Government ITIs through \nPublic Private Partnership \n(\nPPP\n)\n.\n \n \n \n*****\n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_145": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 145* \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON JULY 26, 2017 \n \nDELAYED RESIDENTIAL PROJECTS \nNo. 145*. SHRI P. V. MIDHUN REDDY: \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS be pleased to \nstate: \n (a) whether it is a fact that hundreds of residential projects \nlaunched by a number of builders in urban cities are delayed for \nseveral years;  \n(b)  if so, the details thereof;  \n(c) whether the Government proposes to take over these projects \nand complete the same for the homebuyers; and  \n(d)  if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR) \n \n(a) to (d) : A Statement is laid on the Table of the Sabha. \n \nContd….2.. \n\n \n \n \n-2- \n \nSTATEMENT \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 145* FOR 26.07.2017 REGARDING “DELAYED \nRESIDENTIAL PROJECTS” \n \n(a) & (b): The Ministry does not maintain details of projects \nlaunched by builders in urban areas and delays in their \nexecution. However, in order to bring transparency in \noperations in the real estate sector and to ensure timely \ncompletion of ongoing and new projects the Ministry has \npiloted the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) \nAct, 2016. \n \n(c) & (d): No Madam, there is no such proposal under consideration \nof the Government to take over the delayed residential \nprojects and complete the same for the homebuyers. \n \n \n****\n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_146": "������������������� �\n�������������������� �\n�\n��������� �\n������������������������ �\n���������������������������� �\n�\n�\n������������������������� �\n�\n���� �������������������������� �\n������������������������� � �\n�\n������������������������������������������� ��������������� ������ � �\n�� ���������� ���� ��������� ���� ��������� �� ��� ����� ������ ��� ������\n����� ��� ������� ������������� ���������� ��������� ���� ��������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������� �\n�\n�� ������ ������� ��� ������� ������������� �������� ���� �������� ����������\n���������������������������������������������������� �\n�\n�� ������ ������� ���������� ��� �������� �������� ���������� ���������\n�������������������������� �\n�\n�� ���������� ���� ��������� ������ ��� ������� ���������� �����������\n������ ��������� ���� ��� ���������� ������������� �� ������ ��� ��������\n�������������������������������������������� �\n�\n�� ���������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������� ��� ������ ���� ����������� ��� ������ ���� �������� ���\n����������������� �\n�\n�\n������ �\n�\n��������� �� ���������� �\n������������� ����������������� �\n�\n����������������������������������������������������������� ��\n�\n����� �\n\n��������� � ��������� ��� ��� ����� � ��� ������ ���� �� � ���� ���\n�������� ��������� ��� ����� � ��� ���� ��� ����� ������� ���� �����\n���������� ������� � ��� ��� ��������� ��� ���� ������ ���\n��������������� �������������������� ����������� ��\n�\n����������������������������������������������������������������������\n������� ����� ����������� ��� ����������� ��� �������� ������� ��� �����\n����������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������ ����������� ������������ ������� ��� ����������� ��� �� �����������\n�����\n������������ ���� ������ ���� ������� ������ ������������� �������� ���� ����\n������������������������������������������������ �\n����� ��� ������� ��� ����� ������ ����������������� ���� ���������� �������\n������������������ �\n������������������ �\n����������������������������������������������������� ������������� ���\n���������������������������������������������������������������� �\n� ���� ���������� �������� ������� �������� ������� �������� ������� ����\n� ������� ���� ��� ���� ������� ����� ������������������� ��������� ����\n� ������������������������������������������������� �\n����� ������������ ��� ������� ��� �������� ��� �������� ������� ������ �������\n�������� ��� ��� ����� ��� �������� ������������ ������� ������ ��������\n������������������� �\n����� ����������� ������������ ��������� ��� ������������� ��� �������� ������� ���\n������������ �\n���� ����������������������������������������������������������������������\n���� ���� ��� ���� ���������� � ������ ��� ���� �������� ��� ��� ��� ������\n��������������������\n",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_147": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF MINORITY AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.*147 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 26.07.2017 \n \nGARIB NAWAZ SKILL DEVELOPMENT CENTRES \n \n*147.    SHRI SATAV RAJEEV:  \n SHRI CH. MALLA REDDY: \n   \nWill the Minister of MINORITY AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is planning to offer certificate course in Goods and Services Tax  \n(GST) accounting, programming and other related subjects through its Garib Nawaz Skill \nDevelopment Centres and if so, the details thereof; \n(b) the amount that will be charged from minority students for pursuing this certificate \ncourse; \n(c) the name of the district s where Garib Nawaz Skill Development Centres will be \nestablished and the time by which these Centers will be established in variou s districts of \nthe country; \n(d) whether the Course  will be offered with the assistance of national and international \nexperts on GST and if so, the details thereof; and \n(e) the benefits likely to accrue to the minority students?     \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) IN THE MINISTRY  \nOF MINORITYAFFAIRS \n(SHRI MUKHTAR ABBAS NAQVI ) \n \n \n(a) to (e): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n**** \n  \n\nStatement referred to in reply to part (a) to (e ) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No. * 147 \nasked by Shri  Satav Rajeev and  Shri Ch. Malla Reddy  regarding Garib Nawaz Skill \nDevelopment Centres. \n(a) & (b): Maulana Azad Education Foundation (MAEF) has launched a new scheme namely \nGharib Nawaz Skill Development Training for Minorities  for short term job oriented skill \ndevelopment courses. Awareness and training on GST will also be a component of some of the \ncourses under the scheme .The skill development training courses under the scheme are free of \ncost. \n(c): The f irst Gharib Nawaz Skill D evelopment Centre has been inaugurated at Hyderabad in \ncollaboration with Electronics Corporation of India Limited  (ECIL) and National Institute for \nMicro, Small and medium Enterprises  (NIMSME). While it is planned to establish the centres \naround the country, the districts and location of the same have not been finalized. \n(d) & (e): This scheme willbe implemented through the Programme Implementing Agencies \n(PIAs) as per the approved course curriculum for which qualified teachers and experts, including \nin the  field of GST, will be engaged by the PIAs.  The minority youth will benefit under the \nscheme as it will help them get relevant job related training which will prepare and make them \neligible for job opportunities. \n.    \n******* \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_148": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 148 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 17.07.2017 \n \nCONSTRUCTION WORKERS WELFARE CESS ACT \n148. SHRI B.V. NAIK:  \n        SHRI S.P. MUDDAHANUME GOWDA:  \n \nWill the Minister of LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT be pleased to \nstate:  \n \n(a)the total amount collected and lying idle under the Building and \nOther Construction Workers’ Welfare Cess Act, 1996;  \n(b)the reasons for delay in working o ut utilisation and disbursement \nmechanism for the funds collected under the said Act; and \n(c)the steps taken by the Government to ensure utilization of this fund \nfor the welfare of construction workers? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (IC) FOR LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n(SHRI BANDARU DATTATREYA) \n \n(a) & (b):  The total amount of cess collected by the State \nGovernments/ Union Territory Administrations is approximately         \nRs. 33,602.61 crore out of which Rs. 7601.38  crore has been spent as \non 30.06.2017 and the balance amount of cess lying with the State \nGovernments/ Union Territory Administrations for utilization is approx. \nRs. 26001.23 crore. The Cess fund is being utilized for the welfare of \nthe building and other construction workers by the States/UTs through \ntheir respective State Building and Other Construction Workers \nWelfare Boards constituted under the Building and Other Construction \nWorkers (Regulation of Employment and Conditions of Service) Act, \n1996.   \nContd..2/- \n\n::  2  :: \n(c):   The Central Government has been issuing directions under \nSection 60 of the Building and Other Construction Workers (RECS) \nAct, 1996, to the State  Governments/UT Administrations from time to \ntime for proper utilization of cess fund in terms of the provisions of \nthe Act.   \nFurther, the Central Government has constituted a \nMonitoring Committee o n 09.09.2015 under the Chairmanship of \nSecretary (Labour and Employment) to monitor the implementation of \ndirections issued under Section 60 of the Act, specifically with \nreference to utilization of Cess F und for Welfare Schemes by the State \nBuilding and O ther Construction Workers’ Welfare Boards.  The \nCommittee has been holding regular meetings with the Principal \nSecretary/Secretary/Labour C ommissioners of all the States/ UTs to \nmonitor the progress.   \n \n******* ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_149": "LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.149 \nFOR ANSWER ON 17/07/2017 \n \nNEW STEEL PLANTS \n \n149. SHRIMATI KOTHAPALLI GEETHA: \n \nWill the Minister of STEEL be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes  to set up new Steel plants with Private  \nplayers on PSU lands in the country; and \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof and progress made in this regard, so far plant-wise? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR STEEL         (SHRI VISHNU DEO SAI) \n \n(a) There is no proposal.  \n(b) Does not arise, in view of (a) above.  \n \n******** \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_15": "1 \n \n \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF SCHOOL EDUCATION & LITERACY \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.15 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 17.07.2017 \n \nUPGRADATION OF NAVODAYA VIDYALAYAS \n \n*15. SHRI RAM CHARAN BOHRA:  \n \nWill the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has any proposal to upgrade the Navodaya Vidyalayas \nup to graduation levels; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor; and \n(d) the details about the academic performance of Navodaya Vidyalayas, Kendriya \nVidyalayas and other autonomous bodies along with employability of students \nduring the last three years? \n \nANSWER \n \n \nMINISTER OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n(SHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKAR) \n \n \n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n \n**** \n \n  \n\n2 \n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO THE PARTS (a) to (d) OF LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO.15 TO BE ANSWERED ON 17.07.2017 \nREGARDING UPGRADATION OF NAVODAYA VIDYALAYAS \n \n(a) to (c) The Jawahar Navodaya Vidyalayas (JNVs) are set up to provide quality modern \neducation from Classes VI to XII to the talented children predominantly from rural areas. \nThese are the best institutes in School Sector. \n \n(d) The academic performance (pass perc entage) of students of Jawahar Navodaya \nVidyalayas (JNVs), Kendriya Vidyalayas (K Vs), Central Tibetan Schools Administration \n(CTSA) schools and other Central Board of S econdary Education (CBSE) affiliated schools \nduring the last three years is as under: \n \n \nAcademic Performance- Class X \nYear JNVs KVs  CTSA \nSchools \nOther CBSE Affiliated Schools \nGovernment \nSchools \nGovernment \nAided \nSchools \nIndependent \nSchools \n2014-15 99.76 99.33 96.74 91.84 90.41 98.60 \n2015-16 98.87 98.85 87.34 86.61 85.62 97.72 \n2016-17 99.68 99.66 95.00 70.45 89.10 97.43 \n \n \nAcademic Performance- Class XII \nYear JNVs KVs  CTSA \nSchools \nOther CBSE Affiliated Schools \nGovernment \nSchools \nGovernment \nAided \nSchools \nIndependent \nSchools \n2014-15 96.82 94.72 91.31 86.11 84.42 81.08 \n2015-16 96.69 95.43 87.73 83.85 85.75 82.40 \n2016-17 95.73 94.60 83.57 82.29 81.63 79.27 \n \n \nSince the schools are only up to Class XII, the data regarding the employability ratio of the \nstudents is not maintained.  \n \n*** ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_150": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.150 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 26.07.2017 \n \n SMART STATIONS \n \n*150. SHRI RAM CHARITRA NISHAD: \n       SHRI B. SRIRAMULU: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n      \n(a) whether the Government has joined hands with the National \nBuilding Construction Corporation for re -development of 10 railway \nstations across the country on global standards and if so, the details \nthereof;  \n(b) whether the Ministry of Housing  and Urban Affairs, which had \nlaunched a mega project of developing 100 cities as smart cities, \njoined the Railways in re -developing stations as smart stations and if \nso, the details thereof;  \n(c) whether the Railways has embarked on an ambitious project to re-\ndevelop 403 stations with the participation of private players, public \nsector and foreign agencies and if so, the details thereof;  \n(d) whether the Government has launched cloud based rail display \nnetwork across the country and if so, the details thereof; and \n(e) whether the Government has invited private companies to become \nthe partner in above project, if so, the detailed terms and conditions \nthereof and the steps being taken by the Government for use of \nmodern information and communication technologies in Railways? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI SURESH PRABHAKAR PRABHU) \n \n \n \n(a) to (e): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n**** \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.150 BY SHRI RAM CHARITRA NISHAD AND \nSHRI B. SRIRAMULU TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON \n26.07.2017 REGARDING SMART STATIONS \n \n(a) & (b): The Government of India has launched schemes of ‘SMART \nCities’ and Atal  Mission for Rejuvenation and Urban Transformation \n(AMRUT) for the redevelopment and rejuvenation of the cities with a \npopulation of more than 1 lakh and covering Capitals of all States \nand Union Territories. With a view to providing the cities covered in \nthese schemes with a redeveloped railway station which is \nintegratedly planned with the surrounding parts of their cities, a \nMemorandum of Understanding (MoU) has been signed between \nMinistry of Railways (MOR) and Ministry of Urban Development \n(MOUD) for m utual cooperation between the two Ministries for \nintegrated planning of redevelopment of railway stations in the \ncities included in these schemes. This would lead to development of \nintegrated public transit hub around the railway stations and \nencourage Transit Oriented Development.  \nEach Smart City has incorporated a Special Purpose Vehicle \n(SPV) to execute the Smart City Plan. The SPV may form a joint \nventure company with an MOR -designated entity to implement \nrailway station redevelopment projects in that city and in its \nsuburbs.   \n Another form of joint venture could be between the MOR \ndesignated entity, the Smart City SPV and the National Building \nConstruction Corporation Ltd. (NBCC), a Public Sector Undertaking \nunder MOUD.   \n\nAccordingly, an MoU  between RLDA and NBCC has been \nsigned on 30.06.2017 for development of following 10 stations under \nthis MoU and the process will be further taken up. \n \nSr \nNo \nStation Category",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_151": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ELECTRONICS  AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.  *151 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON: 26.07.2017 \n \n \nSHIFTING OF BPO COMPANIES TO RURAL AREAS \n  \n \n*151.     SHRI CHANDRA PRAKASH JOSHI:  \n                     \nWill the Minister of Electronics and Information Technology be pleased to state: \n(a) whether BPO companies are shifting their operations to rural areas of the country for \ntapping talent to run cost-effective operations; \n(b) if so, the details thereof along with the status of the project; \n(c) whether the Government is offering certain incentives to such compan ies to attract \nthem to operate from rural India; and \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER FOR  ELECTRONICS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n(SHRI RAVI SHANKAR PRASAD) \n \n(a) to (d):   A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n  \n\n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. *151 \nFOR 26.07.2017 REGARDING  SHIFTING OF BPO COMPANIES TO RURAL AREAS \n……..  \n \n \n(a) and (b): Yes, Sir.  As per National Association of Software and Services \nCompanies (NASSCOM), the Indian BPO companies are setting up centres in non-metro cities and \nrural areas of the country to run cost -effective operations. Over the last few years, many small and \nlarge BPO companies have significantly enhanced their presence in non -metro locations including \nrural areas. The Indian BPO industry provides employment to about 10 lakh persons in BPO sector \nincluding more than 50% persons from the talent pool of non-metro locations.   \n \n(c) and (d):  Under Digital India programme, the Government has launched two BPO promot ion \nschemes namely India BPO Promotion Scheme (IBPS) and North East BPO Promotion Scheme \n(NEBPS), for creation of employment opportunities and promotion of investment in Information \nTechnology and Information Technology Enabled Services (IT/ITES) sector ac ross the country \nparticularly in small cities/towns including rural areas, by incentivizing setting up of 48,300 and \n5,000 seats BPO/ITES operations  with an outlay of  `493 crore and  `50 crore respectively.   \n \nThese schemes provide capital support along with special incentives like encouraging employment \nto women and physically disabled persons, promoting local entrepreneurs etc. upto `1 lakh/seat in \nthe form of Viability Gap Funding (VGF).   \n \nUnder IBPS, till d ate 87 companies have entered into preliminary agreement with Software \nTechnology Parks of India (STPI, Implementing Agency of IBPS) to setup BPO/ITES operations \nfor a total of 18,160 seats distributed around 63 locations covering 19 States and 2 UTs.   \n \nUnder NEBPS, till date 11 companies have entered into preliminary agreement with STPI to setup \nBPO/ITES operations for a total of 1,610 seats distributed around 7 locations covering 5 States  of \nNorth East Region (NER). \n \nFurther, details of these schemes are  available at https://ibps.stpi.in, www.meity.gov.in/ibps and \nwww.meity.gov.in/nebps   \n \n******* \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_152": "Page 1  of 2  \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY\n \nDEPARTMENT OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY\n \nLOK SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.152\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 26/07/2017\n \n \nLAUNCHING OF MOBILE APP\n \n \n*152.\n \nSHRI C. MAHENDRAN:\n \n \nWill the Minister of SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY\n \nÉÊ´ÉYÉÉxÉ A´ÉÆ |ÉÉètÉÉäÉÊMÉBÉEÉÒ àÉÆjÉÉÒ\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a)\n \nwhether the Government has recently launched a Mobile App to popularize yoga tradition;\n \n \n(b)\n \nif so, the details thereof;\n \n \n(c)\n \nwhether this provides a platform to share information and insig\nhts about peoples' \nparticipation in yoga events and activities; and\n \n \n(d)\n \nif so, the details thereof?\n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER FOR MINISTRY OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY AND MINISTRY OF EARTH \nSCIENCES\n \n(DR. HARSH VARDHAN)\n \nÉÊ´ÉYÉÉxÉ A´ÉÆ |ÉÉètÉÉäÉÊMÉBÉEÉÒ àÉÆjÉÉÒ +ÉÉè® {Éßl´ÉÉÒ ÉÊ´ÉYÉÉxÉ àÉÆjÉÉÒ \n \n(bÉ. c­ÉÇ ´ÉvÉÇxÉ)\n \n \n \n(a) to (d\n):  A statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n \n\nPage 2  of 2  \nSTATEMENT AS REFE\nRRED IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d\n) OF L\nOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO.152\n \nFOR 26/07/\n2017 REGARDING \nLAUNCHING OF MOBILE APP\n \n \n(a)     \nYes, Madam. Vigyan Prasar, an autonomous institution under the \nDepartment of Science and \nTechnology (DST), has developed a \nMobile App \"Celebrating Yoga \n-\n \nConnecting People with \nHealth and Life\".\n \n(b)     The \nHon'ble Minister for Science & Technology and Earth Sciences, Dr. Harsh Vardhan, \nlaunched the Mobile App at New Delhi on 19\nth\n \nJune, 2017\n. It was developed on the occasion of the \nInternational Yoga Day 2017. The purpose of the App is to popularize Yoga and \nencourage people \nto practice \nand derive benefits from it. The Application is available to all citizens free of cost from the \nGoogle Store.\n \nAs it aims at improving the health and quality of life, the App is aligned to the \n\"Swasth \nBharat\" Mission of the \nGovernment of India. \n \n(c) & (d): \nYes\n,\n \nMadam. The App provides a platform for sharing information by \ncapturing the mass \nevents being organized in public places, \nschools and office complexes across the country and also \nefforts of individual enthusiasts who \nc\nontribute towards promoting yoga and its benefits.\n \nP\neople who \npractice yoga and wish to share their own \nyoga posture photographs with others can also use this App \nand upload their photographs. The App is connected to the Google Map where shared information\n \ncan be seen by the users. With user’s permission, the application automatically collects the location \ndata from the phone\n \nand shows \nfrom where the information was sent using a marker on the Google \nmap.\n \n********\n ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_153": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 153 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 17.07.2017 \n \nEngineering Colleges  \n \n†153. SHRIMATI JAYSHREEBEN PATEL: \nWill the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n(a) the number of Government and private engineering colleges in the country \nand the total number of seats in these engineering colleges, State/UT-wise; \n(b) the number of seats filled up and lying vacant in these colleges and the \nreasons for seats lying vacant; \n(c) whether it is a fact that a committee has been constituted to conduct inquir y \nin this regard; and \n(d) if so, the details thereof and the me asures being taken by the Government \nin this regard? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n \n(DR. MAHENDRA NATH PANDEY) \n \n(a) & (b): The number of Government an d Private engineering colleges in the \ncountry, total number of seats therein for the Academic Year 2016-17 & 2017-18 and \nthe number of seats lying vacant for the Academic Year 2016-17 are at Annexure I-\nIV. The filling up of seats in the engine ering colleges depends on demand-supply \nsituation which is attributable to location of the college, level of facilities in the \ninstitute and the placement opportunities. \n(c): No, Madam. \n(d): Does not arise. \n \n********* \n \n \n \n\n \nANNEXURES AS REFERRED TO IN PART (a) & (b) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 153 DATED \n17.07.2017 ASKED BY SHRIMATI JAYSHREEBEN PATEL REGARDING ENGINEERING COLLEGES  \nAnnexure-I \nENGINEERING & TECHNOLOGY(UG,PG) GOVERNMENT INSTITUTES 2016-17 \nSTATE/UT APPROVED INSTITUTES APPROVED INTAKE ENROLLMENT % OF VACANT SEATS \nAndaman and Nicobar \nIslands \n1 90 91 0.00 \nAndhra Pradesh 16 5238 3303 36.94 \nArunachal Pradesh 1 18 0 100.00 \nAssam 11 2649 2066 22.01 \nBihar 16 4178 2834 32.17 \nChandigarh 5 1523 968 36.44 \nChhattisga