    "ls|LS16_S12_U_214": "1 \n \n \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CULTUE \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.214 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 31.7.2017 \nSHRAVANA 9, 1939 (SAKA) \n \n \nPOLYTHENE FREE ZONE \n \n \n+*214. SHRIMATI BHAVANA PUNDALIKRAO GAWALI PATIL: \nSHRI RAM CHARITRA NISHAD:  \n   \n \n \n Will the Minister of CULTURE be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) the number of historical monuments/temples and other sites protected by the \nArchaeological Survey of India in the country particularly in Maharashtra;  \n(b) the details of the revenue earned from the sale of tickets;  \n(c) whether the  Government proposes to declare all the historical monuments and \nheritage sites as polythene free area and if so, the details thereof; and  \n(d) whether the Government is considering to mark the peripheral area within the \nrange of 500 metres as ‘Polythene Free Zone’ and if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE, CULTURE AND TOURISM (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \n(DR. MAHESH SHARMA) \n \n \n(a)to(d) A statement is laid on the table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n2 \n \n \n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) TO (d) OF THE LOK  SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.214 FOR 31.7.2017 \n \n \n(a) There are 3686 monuments/sites including temples which have been \ndeclared as protected monuments/sites in the country with 285 \nmonuments/sites in Maharashtra.  \n \n(b) The revenue earned from sale of entry t ickets at the centrally protected \nticketed monuments under Archaeological Survey of India during the year \n2016-17 is Rs.221.30 crores.  \n \n(c) The Ministry of Culture has recommended prohibition on use of polythene. \nASI has declared all ASI protected Monume nts and Archaeological Sites as \n‘Polythene Free Zone’.   \n \n(d) No such proposal is under consideration. \n \n \n \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_215": "(c)  \n \nThe Science Cities Scheme provides for setting up of Science Cities \nand Science Centres in all the states of the country, subject to \navailability of funds for this purpose. Stat\nes willing to avail of this \nScheme have to provide land and share the cost of setting up of \nfacility and corpus for upkeep and maintenance.  \n \n \nThe Science Centres set up in the states of Bihar, Jharkhand, \nRajasthan and Gujarat are:\n \n��\n��\n��\n��\nSri Krishna Science Cen\ntre,Patna, \n����������\n��\n2\n.\n \nRegional Science Centre, Ranchi, \n������������������\n \n3\n.\n \nRegional Science Centre, Jaipur, \n������������������\n \n4\n.\n \nSub\n-\nRegional Science Centre, Jodhpur, \n������������������\n \n5\n.\n \nDistrict Science Centre, Dharampur\n��������������������\n \n \nThe proposals to set up Sub Regional Science Centre, Udaipu\nr in \nRajasth\nan, Sub Regional Science Centre\n,\n \nGaya and  Dr. A. P. J. \nAbdul  Kalam Science City, Patna in Bihar have been approved by \nMinistry of Culture. \n \n \nThere is no specific time frame in the Scheme in which Science \nCities/Science Centres are to be set u\np in each State/UT, since setting \nup of a Science City/Science Centre depends on the receipt of a \nproposal from State Government along with commitments for meeting \nrequirements such as land, fund etc.\n \n \n(d) \n \nThe funds allocated and utilized so far by NCSM f\nor setting  up of \nscience centres during 12\nth\n \nPlan period is shown at \n����������������\n��\n��\n��\n��\n(e)   \n \nN\no.\n \n��\n��\n��\n��\n\n��\n������������������������\n��\n��\nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLLY  TO (a) TO (e) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NUMBER * 215 FOR 31.07.2017\n \n \n������������������������������\n��\n��\n��������������\n��\n����������������������������\n����������������������������\n��\n����������\n��\n����������\n����������������\n��\n1\n.\n \n \nRegional Science Centre, Tirupati\n \nAndhra Pradesh\n \n \n2\n.\n \n \nSci