    "ls|LS16_S12_U_218": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF CULTURE\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 218 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 17.07.2017\n \n \nREVITALIZATION OF PUBLIC LIBRARIES\n \n \n218. SHRI KESINENI NANI:\n \n \nWill the \nMinister of CULTURE\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(\na\n)\n \nthe State\n-\nwise list of public li\nbraries in the country;\n \n \n(\nb\n)\n \nwhether any public libraries have been closed over the past three years and if so, the \ndetails thereof, State\n-\nwise;\n \n \n(\nc\n)\n \nwhether the public libraries are facing the problem of revitalizing public libraries; and\n \n \n(\nd\n)\n \nif so, the details of t\nhe plans of the Government to revitalize public libraries?\n \n \n \n(DR. MAHESH SHARMA)\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE, CULTURE \n \nAND TOURISM (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \n \n \nANSWER\n \n \n(a) & (b)\n \nThere are six public libraries under administrative control of Ministry of Culture \nnamely Nat\nional Library, Kolkata, Central Reference Library, Kolkata, Central \nSecretariat Library, New Delhi, Delhi Public Library, Delhi, Khuda Bakhsh Oriental \nPublic Library, Patna and Rampur Raza Library, Rampur.\n \n \nData regarding State\n-\nwise list of Public Librarie\ns is not maintained by Ministry of \nCulture.\n \n \nNone of the public Libraries under the control of Ministry of Culture has been closed \nover past three years. However, the following five sub branch and Resettlement \ncolony libraries of Delhi Public Library have \nbeen closed in 2015 due to lack of \nmembership and the same merged with the nearest sub branch/ zonal Library:\n \n \n1. Jagruthi Enclave Sub branch\n \n2. New Rajinder Nagar Sub branch\n \n3. Netaji Nagar Sub branch\n \n4. Vigyan\n \nVihar Sub branch\n \n5. Wazirpur Resettlement co\nlony Library\n \n\n \n(c)\n \nCentral Government is providing financial help through various matching and non\n-\nmatching schemes of Raja Rammohun Roy Library Foundation and National Mission \non Libraries for the upgradation and modernization of Libraries.\n \n \n(d)\n \nTo revital\nize Public Libraries Ministry of Culture through the matching and non\n-\nmatching schemes of Raja Rammohun Roy Library Foundation and through National \nMission on Libraries is providing financial assistance for various purposes eg \nconstruction/renovation of li\nbrary buildings, upgradation of infrastructure with \nfurniture and equipment, modernization, procurement of books and reading \nresources, organization of seminar/training and capacity building of Library \nprofessionals/workshop/outreach programs, establishmen\nt of children corner, \nopening of various sections, creating facilities for specially\n-\nabled readers, brail corner \netc.\n \n \n***\n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_219": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 219 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 17.07.2017 \n \nStudent Death and Dropout in IITs \n \n219. SHRI DHARAM VIRA:  \n \nWill the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to \nstate:  \n \n(a)  whether the Government is aware of the number of student’ deaths and \ndrop out rates of Indian Institutes of Technology (IITs);  \n \n(b)  if so, the details of such inst ances reported in the current year, \nInstitution-wise and the reasons therefor; and  \n \n(c)  whether the students in IITs are en couraged to join de-stressing and other \nmotivational/ psychological activities for total personality development \nand if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n(DR. MAHENDRA NATH PANDEY) \n \n \n(a) to (c) : During the current academic year, 8 cases of death have been \nreported, which include 4 unnatural and 4 accidental deaths in various IITs. \nIITs have been taking various steps such as appointment of Student Counselors, \norganizing Workshops/Seminars on Ha ppiness/Wellness, regular sessions on \nYoga, holding induction programs, extrac urricular activities including sports \nand cultural activities etc. to de-stress the students and for their overall \npersonality development.  As regards drop-outs, a total of 889 students dropped \nout from various pgorammes in IITs, whic h include 630 in Postgraduate, 196 in \nPh.D and 63 in Undergraduate programme s. The main reasons for Ph.D. and \nPostgraduate students leaving the course s midway are the offers for placement \nin Public Sector Enterprises, and person al preference for be tter opportunities \nelsewhere. The drop out in Undergra duate programmes is attributed to \nwithdrawal due to wrong choices filled, poor performance and personal reasons. \nDetails of deaths and drop-outs in each IITs are annexed.       \n***** \n\n \nANNEXURE \n \nREFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 219 TO BE ANSWERED ON 17.07.2017 REGARDING \n“STUDENT DEATH AND DROPOUT IN IITs” ASKED BY SHRI DHARAM VIRA: \nDetails of student’s death in IITs \nSl. \nNo.  \nName of the \ninstitute  \nNo. of \nstudent \ndeath  \nReasons of death  \n1. IIT Kharagpur 03 All the death cases were unnatural and the \nfinal reports from the police have not been \nreceived. \n2. IIT Madras 01 Accident.  \n3. IIT Roorkee 01 Accident. \n4. IIT BHU Varanasi 01 Committed suicide. \n5. IIT Bhubaneswar 01 Died on 24.10.2016 due to asphyxia caused \nby drowning under sea water (Bay of Bengal).   \n6. IIT Mandi 01 Died due to drowning in the river. \n \nDetails of student’s dropout in IITs \nSl. No.  Name of the institute  Number of dropout \nUG PG Ph.D Total \n1. IIT Kharagpur 12  82 0 94  \n2. IIT Bombay 0  52 19 71  \n3. IIT Delhi 3  180 0 183  \n4. IIT Kanpur 15  140 0 155  \n5. IIT Madras 0  0 0 0  \n6. IIT Guwahati 3  0 0 3  \n7. IIT Roorkee 25  112 102 239  \n8. IIT BHU(Varanasi) 0  0 0 0  \n9. IIT Hyderabad 01  35 24 60  \n10. IIT Jodhpur 0  0 04 04  \n11. IIT Gandhinagar 0  0 0 0  \n12. IIT Bhubaneswar 0  16 15 31  \n13. IIT Patna 0  8 11 19  \n14. IIT Indore 01  5 12 18  \n15. IIT Ropar 2  0 0 2  \n16. IIT Mandi 0  0 09 9  \n17. IIT Palakkad 01  0 0 1  \n Total 63  630 196 889  \n18. IIT Tirupati  \nNo Drop Outs \n19. IIT Bhilai \n20. IIT Goa \n21. IIT Dharwad \n22. IIT Jammu \n23. IIT (ISM) Dhanbad \n*****\n\n ",
