    "ls|LS16_S12_U_229": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TOURISM \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.229 \nANSWERED ON 17.07.2017 \n \nFUNDS SANCTIONED UNDER PRASAD SCHEME  \n \n229.  SHRIMATI P.K. SREEMATHI TEACHER:  \n \nWill the Minister of TOURISM be pleased to state:  \n \n(a)  whether the Government has taken up any work in the State of \nKerala to be implemented under PRASAD Scheme and if so, \nthe details thereof;  \n(b)  the details of the proposals recommended by the Government \nof Kerala;  \n(c)  the details of the funds sanctioned and released so far , \ndistrict-wise; and  \n(d)  the status of works as on date?  \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR TOURISM (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \n(DR. MAHESH SHARMA) \n \n(a): Yes madam. The Ministry of Tourism has included “Guruvayur \nTemple” for development of infrastructure facilities  under its \nscheme viz.  Pilgrimage Rejuvenation and Spiritual Augmentation \nDrive (PRASAD). The project at a total estimated cost of Rs. 46.14 \ncrore has been approved in 2016-17.  \n \n(b): This was the only proposal received from the State \nGovernment of Kerala f or inclusion under PRASAD Schem e.  \nHowever, the Ministry of Tourism under spiritual circuit theme of \nSwadesh Darshan Scheme has sanctioned following projects for \ndevelopment at Sabrimala in 2016-17: \n \n1.  Development of Sabarimala - Erumeli- Pampa- \nSannidhanam as a Spir itual Circuit in Kerala for Rs. 99.99 \nCrore.  \n\n2.  Development of Sree Padmanabhaswamy - Arnamula-\nSabarimala-as a Spir itual Circuit in Kerala for Rs. 92.44 \nCrore. \n \n(c) & (d): The details of the funds released and the status of works \nfor the proje ct under PRASAD and Swadesh Darshan Schemes are \ngiven below. \n                                                                     (Rs. in crore) \nSl. \nNo. \nName of The Project Funds \nReleased \nStatus of work as \non date \nPRASAD Scheme: \n1. Guruvayur Temple under  the \nPRASAD Scheme \n9.23 Under \nimplementation \nSWADESH DARSHAN Scheme:  \n1. Development of Sabarimala - \nErumeli- Pampa- Sannidhanam \nas a Spiritual Circuit in Kerala  \n20.00 Under \nimplementation \n2. Development of Sree \nPadmanabhaswamy - \nArnamula-Sabarimala-as a  \nSpiritual Circuit in Kerala \n18.49 Under \nimplementation \n \n********* \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_23": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 23 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 17.07.2017 \n \nINCENTIVES TO HAZARDOUS SECTOR WORKERS \n †23. SHRI NAGAR RODMAL:  \nWill the Minister of LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT be pleased to \nstate:  \n(a)the details of schemes being implemented by the Government for \nproviding incentives to labourers engaged in hazardous works; and  \n(b)the number and details of labourers working in the labour sector \nwho have been provided incentives under these schemes duri ng the \nlast three years and the current year, scheme -wise and State/UT -\nwise? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (IC) FOR LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n(SHRI BANDARU DATTATREYA) \n \n(a) & (b): For securing the safety and health of workers working in \nhazardous process industries registered under Factories Act, 1948, \nadequate safeguards are available in the Act and the State Factories \nRules framed thereunder. However, no specific schemes are being  \nimplemented for providing incentives to labourers engaged in \nhazardous works by Ministry of Labour & Employment.   \n \n****** ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_230": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *230 \n \n TO BE ANSWERED ON THE 01ST AUGUST, 2017 / SHRAVANA 10, 1939 (SAKA) \n \n   EXPANSION OF MAOIST REGION \n \n  *230.  SHRI HUKUM SINGH: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:    \n \n(a) whether the Maoists have been  attempting to create an entirely new zone  of \noperations along the western border of the country; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) whether the Maoists are expa nding their region in districts of such States as  \nMadhya Pradesh, Maharashtra and  Chhattisgarh as compared to their earlier  \nregion in forested pockets and if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(d) the steps being taken by the  Government to win over villagers on  various \nissues such as land, differential pricing of  bamboo in different States and  \ndemonetisation? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HANSRAJ GANGARAM AHIR) \n \n(a) to (d):   A statement is laid on the table of the House.  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n--2-- \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION \nNUMBER *230 FOR 01 AUG 2017  \n \n(a) to (c). Change of tactics, in areas of operation and tactics is a constant and \non-going effort of insurgent groups such as Left Wing Extremists. No significant \nchange in the pattern of frequency or geography of violence or activity has \nhowever been reported from States such as Madhya Pradesh, Maharashtra and \nChhattisgarh in the recent past. \n(d). The Government remains in constant touch with the people  through public \nrepresentatives, the democratic system and the administrative machinery to \nkeep them informed with regard to decisions of the Government. \n****** ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_231": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SOCIAL JUSTICE AND EMPOWERMENT \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.  †*231 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 01.08.2017 \n \nINCLUSION OF GADEET NAGAURI CASTE IN OBC LIST  \n \n†*231. SHRI HARISH MEENA:  \n \nWill the Minister of SOCIAL JUSTICE AND EMPOWERMENT be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to include Gadeet Nagauri backward caste of Rajasthan \nin the Central list of Other Backward Classes (OBCs); and  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF SOCIAL JUSTICE AND EMPOWERMENT \n(SHRI THAAWARCHAND GEHLOT) \n \n \n(a) to (b): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n \n***** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) AND (b)  OF \nLOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 231 TO BE ANSWERED O N \n01.08.2017 \n \n(a) and (b): No, Sir.   The issue of inclusion of caste/community ‘Nagori (Muslim)' for \nthe State of Rajasthan as synonym of ‘Gadeet Nagaur i’ was considered by the \nNational Commission for Backward Classes (NCBC) and  the request to include it in \nCentral List of Other Backward Classes  was rejecte d by the NCBC vide Advice No. \n72/Rajasthan/2015 dated 14.07.2015. \nThe NCBC further clarified that the said caste/comm unity is not found either in \nthe list prepared by Mandal Commission or the Centr al List of Other Backward \nClasses for any other State. \n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_232": " \n \nORIGINAL IN HINDI \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \nDEPARTMENT OF FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 232 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18TH JULY, 2017 \n \nLABOUR ISSUES IN FCI \n \n232.  SHRI HARISHCHANDRA CHAVAN: \n \nWill the Minister of CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND PUBLIC \nDISTRIBUTION miHkksDrk ekeys] [kk| vkSj lkoZtfud forj.k ea=h   be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether any investigation has  been done in regard to handing over  \npermanent light duty to handling labourer  in a godown of Food Corporation of \nIndia at Manmad; \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n(c)  the outcome of the said investigation so far? \n \n \nA N S W E R \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR  CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n(SHRI C. R. CHAUDHARY) \n(a):  Yes, Madam. Investigation for allotment of permanent light duty to \nhandling labourers at Food Corporation of India, District office, Manmad was \nconducted. \n \n(b)&(c):  On investigation, 13 genuine cases verified by the Civil Surgeon, \nNasik were recommended for allocation of permanent light duty.   \n \n**** \n \n ",
