    "ls|LS16_S12_U_238": "O.I.H.\n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, \nCOOPERATION\n \n& FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n238\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n1\nST\n \nAUGUST, 2017\n \n \n \nCOLD STORAGES\n \n \n*238. SHRI RAM CHARAN BOHRA: \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS \nWELFARE   \n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \n½ãâ¨ããè\n \n \n \nbe pleased to state\n:\n \n \n(a)\n \n \nthe details of the cold storages established in the country from the grants provided \nby the Union Government, Statewise; and \n \n \n(b) \n \nwhether \nthe Union Government proposes to launch a scheme for providing grants \nfor establishing cold storages for agricultural crops and if so, the details thereof?\n \n \n \nANSWER\n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n  \n½ãâ¨ããè\n \n \n \n \n  \n(SHRI RADHA\n \nMOHAN SINGH\n)\n \n \n \n(a) & (b\n):\n \nA statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO \nIN REPLY TO PARTS (a) \n& \n(\nb\n) OF L\nOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n  \n238\n   \nDUE FOR REPLY ON\n  \n1\nST\n \nAUGUST, 2017\n.\n \n(a) \n&\n \n(b)\n:\n \n \nFor storage and post harvest infrastructure of perishable agriculture crops \nlike fruits, vegetables, flowers, spices, Government is implementing Mission for Integrated \nDevelopment of Horticulture (MIDH) which includes assistance for establishment of \nvario\nus cold chain components i. e. packhouse, pre\n-\ncooling, staging cold room, cold \nstorage, reefer transport and ripening chamber etc. The component is implemented \nthrough sub schemes of National Horticulture Board (NHB), National Horticulture Mission \n(NHM) an\nd Horticulture Mission for North East & Himalayan States (HMNEH).\n \n \n \nThe component is demand/entrepreneur driven for which assistance @ 35% in \nGeneral areas and @ 50% in hilly and scheduled areas is available under MIDH. At \npresent there are 7543 cold stora\nges \n \nwith capacity of 34.67 million \nMT in the country, out \nof which \n4392 cold storages with capacity of 19.47 million MT have been created              \nunder MIDH. Statewise list of projects sanctioned under MIDH is at \nAnnexure \n-\n \nI\n.\n \n \n \n   \nDepartment of \nAgriculture, Cooperation & Farmers Welfare is also implementing \nAgricultural Marketing Infrastructure (AMI) a sub scheme of Integrated Scheme for \nAgricultural Marketing (ISAM) to improve/create scientific storage capacity for farm \nproduce, processed farm p\nroduce and agricultural inputs etc., to reduce post harvest and \nstorage losses. The scheme has two components (i) storage infrastructure and (ii) \nmarketing infrastructure other than storage.\n \n \n \n  \nUnder AMI sub\n-\nscheme, stand alone cold storage projects are n\not admissible for \nsubsidy. However, cold storage as a part of a permissible integrated value chain project \nare eligible for subsidy provided the cold storage component is not more than 75% of Total \nFinancial Outlay (TFO). \n \n \n    \nFurther, Ministry of Food Pr\nocessing Industries (MoFPI) is implementing Kisan \nSAMPADA Yojana, which includes component of creation of integrated cold chain. \nStatewise list of cold chain projects sanctioned under this scheme is at \nAnnexure \n–\n \nII\n.\n \n\nAnnexure \n–\n \nI\n \nState wis\ne cold storage projects sanctioned  under National Horticulture Board (NHB) and National Horticulture Mission (NHM) (sub sche\nmes of MIDH) \nupto 31.03.2017\n \n \n \n \n \n \n(Rs. in lakh)\n \nS.No.\n \n \n \nName of the \n \nState\n \nNHB\n \nNHM\n \nTotal MIDH (NHB and NHM)\n \n1999\n-\n2000 to 2016\n-\n17 \n \n2005\n-\n06 to 2016\n-\n17\n \n \n \nNo.\n \nCapacity (MT)\n \nSubsidy \n \nNo.\n \nCapacity (MT)\n \nSubsidy \n \nNo.\n \nCapacity (MT)\n \nSubsidy \n \n1\n \nAndhra Pradesh\n \n128\n \n628487.42\n \n571