    "ls|LS16_S12_U_5": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TOURISM \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.5 \nANSWERED ON 17.07.2017 \n \nDEVELOPMENT OF INSTA GUIDE APP  \n \n5.  SHRIMATI KOTHAPALLI GEETHA:  \n \nWill the Minister of TOURISM be pleased to state:  \n \n(a)  whether the Government has develop ed Insta Guide Mobile \nApp for the promotion of tourism; and  \n(b)  if so, the details thereof and the response received so far to \nthe App? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR TOURISM (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \n(DR. MAHESH SHARMA) \n \n(a): No, Madam. \n \n(b): Does not arise. \n \n******* ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_50": "LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 50 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 17TH JULY, 2017 \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT IN PETROLEUM SECTOR \n \n+50. SHRI DEVJI M. PATEL \n�������������������������������� �� �������������������������\nWill the Minister of PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS be pleased to state: \n(a) the steps taken by the Government for the skill development under Skill \nIndia initiatives in the petroleum sector during the year 2016 -17 along with \nthe allocation of funds for the same and number of persons included in the \nprogramme and the activities pro posed under Skill India initiatives during \n2017-18; and  \n(b) the number of youths from Jalore, Sirohi and Barmer district of \nRajasthan included under Skill India initiatives? \n \nANSWER \n�������������������������������� �� �������������������������������������������������������� �������������������������������������������������������� �\nMINISTER OF STATE  (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) IN THE MINISTRY OF \nPETROLEUM & NATURAL GAS (SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n(a) The steps taken by the Government in 2016 -17 for skill development in \nthe petroleum sector were: \n(i)  Registration of the Hydrocarbon Skill Sector Council (HSSC) under the \nSocieties Registration Act, 1860. \n(ii) Signing of an MoU by the Ministry of Petroleum and Natural Gas with \nthe Ministry of Skill Development & Entrepreneurship for providing an \nappropriate skill development framework for supply of skilled manpower. \nThe expenditure on Skill Development in the Oil and Gas sector is being \nborne by the PSU’s under the Ministry. As reported by HSSC 3 Skill \nDevelopment Institutes (SDI) were set up as societies under the Societies \nRegistration Act, at Bhubaneswar (Odisha), Kochi (Kerala) and  \nVishakhapatnam (A.P.). Till 31st March 2017, 338 youth were trained in 10 \ntrades at SDI Vishakhapatnam; 84 youth in 2 trades in SDI Bhubaneswar. \n(b) As reported by HSSC no youth from Jalore, Sirohi and Barmer district of \nRajasthan were imparted training in the oil and gas sector Skill \nDevelopment Institutes. This Ministry is, however, does not have \ninformation about trainings conducted by other Ministr ies or any other \ninstitutes where youth from the above districts have been trained. \n-------------�",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_51": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA                                                                                                            \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \nLOK SABHA                                                                                                                                 \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.51                                                                                                                \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19.07.2017 \n \n         NEW ELEVATED CORRIDOR \n \n †* 51     SHRI  RAJAN VICHARE : \n                 Will the Minister of RAILWAYS  be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the construction of new elevated corridor between Airoli \nand Kalwa under the Mumbai Urban Transport Project has not \nbegun as on date; and \n \n(b)   if so, the reasons for delay therein and the time by which it is likely \nto be started along with the details of the estimated expenditure \nthereon? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI SURESH PRABHAKAR PRABHU) \n \n \n(a) and (b) :  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n \n \n \n******** \n \n \n \n \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) AND (b) OF \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 51 BY SHRI RAJAN VICHARE TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 19.07.2017 REGARDING NEW ELEVATED \nCORRIDOR \n \n(a) and (b):   The work for new elevated rail corridor between Airoli and \nKalwa under MUTP -III has been taken up and there is no delay. The \npreliminary Engineering works involving final location survey, \nsubmission of land acquisition proposals to Collector and Geo \nTechnical Investigations have been completed. Baseline Socio \nEconomic S urvey for Project Affected Persons (PAP) has been taken \nup. Tender for construction of Dighe station, subway and bridges at an \napproximate cost of ` 107.20 crore has been invited.   The estimated \ncompletion cost of project is ` 476 crore. \n \n********* \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_52": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \nDEPARTMENT OF INDUSTRIAL POLICY & PROMOTION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 52. \nTO BE ANSWERED ON MONDAY, THE  17TH JULY, 2017. \n \nENGINEERING CLUSTERS UNDER MIIUS \n \n52.  SHRI HARISHCHANDRA CHAVAN: \n \nWill the Minister of COMMERCE AND INDUSTRY be pleased to state: \n                वाणिज्‍ य‍वव ‍द्यग ‍ं ्री \n(a)  whether the Government has set  up Engineering Cluster in Nashik district  of \nMaharashtra under the Modified Industrial Infrastructure Upgradation Scheme \n(MIIUS);  \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(c)  the amount sanctioned/allocated/  released and utilised so far for the said  \ncluster; and \n \n(d)  the details of the progress works carried out by the said cluster? \n \nANSWER \n \nवाणिज्‍ य‍वव ‍द्यग ‍ााज्‍ यं ्री‍स्‍‍ वतं ्‍्रभााा(स्रींतंरी‍िरंमलाा‍ीरीतंाांि(‍ \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \n(SHRIMATI NIRMALA SITHARAMAN) \n \n(a):  Yes Madam.  Department of Industrial Policy &  Promotion (DIPP) \nunder Ministry of Commerce and Industry has set up ‘Nashik \nEngineering Cluster’  in Nashik district of Maharashtra under the parent \nscheme of ‘ Modified Industrial Infrastructure Upgradation Scheme \n(MIIUS)’ which was known as ‘Industrial I nfrastructure Upgradation \nScheme (IIUS)’.  \n \n(b) & (c):  Details of the project is given below: \n \nName of \nproject \nDate of \nApproval \nProject \nCost \nCentral Grant Released \ncentral \ngrant and \nutilized \nDate of \ncompletion \n(Rs. in crore) \nNashik \nEngineering \nCluster, \nMaharashtra \n11.03.2008 67.26 42.87 42.45 12.04.2013 \n \n \n(d): The project at Nasik Engineering Cluster (NEC) has been completed and \nNEC has created world class common industrial infrastructure like ‘Rapid \nPrototype Development centre’, Training centre along with well -equipped \ntraining studio and work stations, and a Calibration & Testing facility which \nhas been accredited by National Accreditation Board for Laboratories \n(NABL).  \n*****  ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_53": "������������������� �\n������������������� �\n�\n��������� �\n�� �������������������� �������\n������������ ����� ����� �\n�\n���������������������������������� �\n�\n������������������������������������������������� �\n�\n�������������������������������������������������� �\n�\n����� �������� ���� ���� ������� ��� ������� �������� ��������� ����\n����������� �������� ��� ���� ����������� ������ ���� �������� ��� ����\n��������� �\n����� �����������������������������\n����� �������� ���� ����������� ��� �������������� ��� ���� ����������\n�������������������������������������������������� �������������\n����������������������������� �\n����� ��������������������������� �\n������ �\n�\n�������������������������������������������������� �\n������������������� �\n�\n������������ ����������� ���� ������������ ��� ���������� ���� �������\n���������� ��������� ��������� ��� ������ ��� ��� ��������� �����������\n������������������������������������������������������������������\n���� �������� ����� ������ ��� ���� ��������������� ��� ���������������\n���������������������� �\n�\n� �������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������� �������������������������������������������������������\n��� ���� ���������� ���� ����������� ������ ��� ��� �������� �������� ����\n������ ��������� ������������ �������� ��������� �������� ���� �������\n���������������������������� �\n�\n� ������������������������������������������� ������������������\n�������������������������������������������������������������� �\n�\n� ��������� ��� �������� ���� ��� ��������� ��� ���� ���������� ��������\n���� ����� �� �������� �������� ������ ��������� ����� ���� ���� ��������� ���\n����������� ���\n������� �",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_54": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF MINORITY AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION No. 54 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19.07.2017 \n \nHaj Subsidy \n \n*54.  SHRI P. NAGARAJAN: \n \nWill the Minister of MINORITY AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the Haj subsidy given by the Union Government during the last three years, \nyear-wise;  \n \n(b) whether the Union Government is in the process of gradually removing Haj \nsubsidy and is contemplating to stop Haj subsidy by the year 2022; and  \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor? \n  \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) IN THE  \nMINISTRY OF MINORITY AFFAIRS \n(SHRI MUKHTAR ABBAS NAQVI) \n \n \n \n(a) to (c)  A statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n \n***** \n  \n\n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) TO (c) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 54 FOR 19.07.2017 RAISED BY SHRI P. NAGARAJAN \nREGARDING HAJ SUBSIDY \n \n(a) to (c ) The responsibility for making air travel arrangements for Haj pilgrims \nidentified by the Haj Committee of India (HCoI) is with Ministry of Civil Aviation \n(MoCA). The pilgrims deposit a fixed amount decided on year to year basis towards \nairfare to HCoI and the balance fare payable to the Airlines is paid by MoCA as \nsubsidy to facilitate the Haj pilgrims. The subsidy given by the Government of India \ntowards air travel of pilgrims for Haj through the Haj Committee of India during last \nthree years is as under: \nYear Total subsidy including service tax  \n(Rs. In crore) \n2014 577.07 \n2015 529.51 \n2016 405.00 \n  \nThe Supreme Court, while dealing with the Special Leave Petition (Civil) No.28609 \nof 2011 vide its judgment  dated 08.05.2012, inter alia observed that Haj subsi dy is \nsomething that is best done away with and directed the central Government to  \nprogressively reduce the amount of subsidy so as to com pletely eliminate it . \nAccordingly, Haj subsidy has been gradually reduced since the year 2013.  \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_55": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA  \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.55  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19.07.2017 \n  \nEVACUATION OF INDIANS FROM QATAR \n \n*55.  SHRI PRALHAD JOSHI: \n \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether Indians have been evacuated from Qatar in the wake \nof the recent political turmoil in the region; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c)  whether there has been any problem with air connectivity ; if \nso, the details thereof and the reasons therefor; \n \n(d) whether additional aircraft have been deployed  for the \npurpose; and \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n(SHRIAMTI SUSHMA SWARAJ) \n \n(a) to (e)  A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n***** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF THE \nLOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 55 REGARDING “EVACUATION \nOF INDIANS FROM QATAR” TO BE ANSWERED ON 19.07.2017 \n \nThere was no need to evacuate any Indian National from Qatar as the situation \nthere was normal.  \n \nTo meet the additional demand for travel due to Eid  and school holiday period \nin June 2017, additional commercial flights were operated by Indian carriers from \nDoha to some cities in India in the light of decision by some Gulf carriers to stop \nflight operations to and fro Doha.  \n \nOne additional daily comme rcial flight was operated between India and Qatar \nbetween 22-25 June as also on 30 June and 1 July.  \n \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_56": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION No. 56 \n(TO BE ANSWERED ON 19.7.2017) \n \n  MISLEADING ADVERTISEMENTS \n \n*56. SHRI RAM KUMAR SHARMA  \n       PROF. PREM SINGH CHANDUMAJRA \n \n \nWill the Minister of INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING be pleased to state:  \na) Whether a sharp rise in turnover of entertainment and advertisement \nindustries has been reported in the country during the last four years;  \n \n(b) if so, the details of the annual turnover of these industries during the years \n2014-15, 2015-16 and 2016-17;  \n \n(c) the segment of the information and broadcasting sector i.e. print, \nelectronic media, wall painting and other which received maximum number of \nadvertisements along with the revenue generated therefrom;  \n \n(d) whether incidents of misleading the common man through these \nadvertisements have come to the light and if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n(e) the corrective action taken by the Government in this regard? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF INFORMATION & BROADCASTING  \n(SMT. SMRITI ZUBIN IRANI) \n \n(a) to (e): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 56 FOR ANSWER ON 19/7/2017   \n \n \n(a) to (c) As per the Report of Indian Media and Entertainment Industry, 2017 \nreleased by Federation of Indian Chambers of Commerce and Industry (FICCI -\nKPMG), the details of annual turnover of the entertainment and advertisement \nindustries alongwith the advertisem ent revenue generated by these industries \namong different segments during the last four years, i.e. from 2013 to 2016 is \nplaced at Annexure. \n \n(d) & (e) As regards in Print Media, Press Council of India (PCI), a statutory \nautonomous organisation under this Ministry has the power to adjudicate the \ncomplaints received by them, under Norms of Journalistic Conduct, 2010 \nemanated from Press Council Act, 1978. The Norms of Journalistic Conduct, \n2010 inter -alia provides that no advertisements shall be published whi ch \npromotes directly or indirectly sale, production or consumption of cigarette, \ntobacco products, wine, alcohol, liquor and other intoxicants. It also inter -alia \nprohibits advertisements having tendency to malign or hurt the religious \nsentiments for offen d the provisions of the Drugs and Magical Remedies \n(Objectionable Advertisement) Act as amended in 2002. Further, PCI has \nreceived 11 complaint cases in 2015 -16 to 2016 -17 pertaining to misleading \nadvertisements.  \n \nAs regards in electronic media, Advertisements telecast on TV channels \nare required to adhere to the Advertising Code prescribed under the Cable TV \nNetworks (Regulation) Act, 1995 and Rules framed thereunder. As per existing \nregulatory framework there is n o pre -censoring on advertisements. Action is \ntaken whenever violation of Code is brought to the notice of the Ministry.  \n \n Rules 7(5) of Cable Television Networks (Regulation) Rules, 1994 \nspecifically provides ‘No advertisement shall contain references which are likely \nto lead the public to infer that the product advertised or any of its ingredients \nhas some special or miracul ous or super -natural property or quality, which is \ndifficult of being proved’. Ministry has constituted an Inter -Ministerial \nCommittee (IMC) to take cognizance suo-motu or to look into specific complaints \nregarding contents on private TV channels. IMC func tions in a recommending \n\ncapacity. This Ministry has received a total of 280 complaints on misleading \nadvertisements during the period 2015 to 2017 (till 30.6.2017).    \n \nAn advisory was issued by the Ministry on 21.8.2014 advising all TV \nchannels not to tel ecast advertisements which were found to be violating \nprovisions of Cable Television Networks Rules, 1994, ASCI Code and also Drugs \n& Magic Remedies (Objectionable Advertisement) Act, 1954.  \n \n The Department of Consumer Affairs have established Grievances Against \nMisleading Advertisement (GAMA) Portal, through which a common man can \nlodge a complaint against misleading advertisements. These complaints are \nprocessed by Advertising Standard Council of India (ASCI) under an MoU with \nDepartment of Consumer Affa irs. The total number of incidents/complaints \nreceived by Department of Consumers during the 2015-16 to 2016-17 is 3368.  \n \n     As part of the self-regulatory initiative of the industry, Advertising Standard \nCouncil of India (ASCI), a regulatory body of ad vertisement industry, self \nregulates advertising content to monitor and decide on complaints against \nadvertisements making misleading, false and unsubstantiated claims.  \n \n \n***** \n\n \nANNEXURE \nANNESURE AS REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF \nTHE LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 56 TO BE ANSWERED \nON 19.07.2017 \nTHE INDIAN MEDIA AND ENTERTAINMENT INDUSTRY SIZE (INR \nBILLION) FOR CALENDAR YEARS 2013 TO 2016: \nMedia \nIndustry \n2013 2014 2015 2016 Growth in 2016 \nover 2015 \nTV 417.2 474.9 542.2 588.3 8.5% \nPrint 243.2 263.4 283.4 303.3 7.0% \nFilms 125.3 126.4 183.2 142.3 3.0% \nDigital \nAdvertising \n30.1 43.5 60.1 76.9 28.0% \nAnimation \nAnd VFX \n39.7 44.9 51.1 59.5 16.4% \nGaming 19.2 23.5 26.5 30.8 16.2% \nOOH 19.3 22.0 24.4 26.1 7.0% \nRadio 14.6 17.2 19.8 22.7 14.6% \nMusic 9.6 9.8 10.8 12.2 13.0% \nTotal 918.1 1025.5 1156.5 1262.1 9.1% \n \n ADVERTISING REVENUE  (INR Billion) \nType of \nMedia \n2013 2014 2015 2016 Growth in 2016 \nover 2015 \nTV 135.9 154.9 181.3 201.2 11.0% \nPrint 162.6 176.4 189.3 201.3 6.3% \nDigital \nAdvertising \n30.1 43.5 60.1 76.9 28.0% \nOut of Home 19.3 22.0 24.4 26.1 7.0% \nRadio 14.6 17.2 19.8 22.7 14.6% \nTotal 362.5 414.0 474.9 528.2 11.2% \n \nA \n\n ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_57": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 57 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19.07.2017 \n \nPOLLUTION-CAUSING COMMODITIES \n \n†* 57. SHRIMATI RAMA DEVI: \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n(a) whether a committee has been constituted to look into the \nprocess of checking pollution in the handling of pollution -\ncausing commodities at sidings and goodsheds; \n(b) if so, the details thereof;  \n(c) the works carried out by the said committee for the purpose; \nand  \n(d) the outcome thereof? \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI SURESH PRABHAKAR PRABHU) \n \n(a) to (d) A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n***** \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 57 BY SHRIMATI RAMA DEVI TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 19.07.2017 REGARDING POLLUTION -\nCAUSING COMMODITIES \n \n(a) & (b) Yes, Madam.  Ministry of Railways have constituted a \nCommittee of two Officers to study and submit report on the extent \nof pollution in handling of pollution intensive co mmodities at sidings \nand goods-sheds and actions to be taken.   \n \n(c) & (d) The Committee has examined the extant instructions, \nrelated documents and existing practice.  Statutory regulations \nhave been referred. The report is in draft stage and is expected to \nbe submitted shortly.  \n \n \n ****** \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_58": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION No. 58 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON JULY 19, 2017 \n \nMULTI-LEVEL PARKING \n \nNo. *58   SHRI SANTOSH KUMAR: \n    DR. RATNA DE (NAG):  \n   \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS be pleased \nto state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government has an y proposal to set up “Multi-level \nParking System” in Delhi/NCR to address the congestion \nproblems; \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof including the plan outlay and the \norganizational set up for the purpose, if any; and \n \n(C) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOUSING AND \nURBAN AFFAIRS \n \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n \n(a) to (c): A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n****** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT \n IN REPLY TO PART (A) TO (C) OF THE LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 58 FOR ANSWER ON  19.07.2017 REGARDING MULTI-\nLEVEL PARKING. \n(a) to (c): The parking facilities in Delhi/NCR are constructed and \nmanaged by respective urban local bodies.  New Delhi Municipal \nCouncil (NDMC) has informed that they have proposals to set up \nthree multi-level parking systems, one each at Kasturba Gandhi \nMarg, Khan Market and Mandir Marg. South Delhi Municipal \nCorporation (SDMC) has informed that there are three projects for \nconstruction of multi-level/stack car  parking at Defence Colony, \nRajouri Garden and Greater Kailash-II at a tentative cost of ₹ 38.00 \ncrores.   East Delhi Municipal Corporation (EDMC) is constructing a \nmulti-level car parking at Krishna Nagar, whi ch is expected to be \ncompleted by March, 2018. Further, multi-level car parking at 12 \nlocations are proposed by EDMC at a cost of ₹ 211.00 crores.  North \nDelhi Municipal Corporation has informed that multi-level/stack \nparking is proposed at 16 different locations in its jurisdiction at a \ntentative cost of ₹ 1080.00 crores.     \n****** ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_59": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.59 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19.07.2017 \n \nRAILWAY SAFETY AUTHORITY \n \n*59.  SHRI  DUSHYANT CHAUTALA:  \n     \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether NITI Aayog, in its latest report, informed that \naccidents due to derailments and at level crossings accounted \nfor 90% of total accidents, 85% casualties and 82% injuries on \nrailway networks; \n \n(b)  if so, the details  thereof; \n \n(c)  whether NITI  Aayog has recommended setting up an \nindependent Railway Safety Authority with statutory backing \nto improve  overall safety situation; and \n \n(d)  if so, the details thereof and the follow -up action taken by the \nGovernment in this regard?  \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI SURESH PRABHAKAR PRABHU) \n(a) to (d):  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n***** \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 59 BY SHRI DUSHYANT CHAUTALA TO BE ANSWERED IN \nLOK SABHA ON 19.07.2017 REGARDING RAILWAY SAFETY AUTHORITY \n \n(a):  Yes, Madam.  These figures have been reported in a note submitted \nby Shri Bibek Debroy, Member NITI Aayog on Fund Deployment \nFramework for Rashtriya Rail Sanraksha Kosh (RRSK) dated 25.04.2017. \n(b):  In the said report it has been m entioned that in the last five years \n(2012-13 to 2016-17) out of total 586 number of accidents, 308 occurred \ndue to derailments, 21 occurred on Manned Level Crossings (MLCs) and \n199 occurred on Unmanned Level Crossings (UMLCs), which together  \naccount  for 90% of total accidents.  In the same period out of total 1011 \nnumber of casualties, 347 occurred due to derailments, 67 on MLC \naccidents and 449 on UMLC accidents which amount to 85% of  total \ncasualties.  The total number of injuries in the said peri od was 1634 out \nof which 944 occurred due to derailments, 58 due to MLC accidents and \n342 due to UMLC accidents which amount to 82% of total injuries.  \n(c) & (d):  Yes, Madam.  In the said report a reference was made to High \nLevel Safety Review Committee ( HLSRC) headed by Dr. Anil Kakodkar \nthat had also suggested  various measures for improving railway safety \nincluding setting up of a Railway Safety Authority (RSA).  Majority of  the \npractical measures suggested by Kakodkar Committee have been \n\nimplemented.  However,   there is no decision to create a Railway Safety \nAuthority. An independent institution namely Commission of Railway \nSafety already functions under the Ministry of Civil Aviation. It \ndischarges the  functions of  review/approval of safety aspects in  \nRailways independently.  \n****** ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_6": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *6 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 17th JULY, 2017 \n \nWORKING PAPER OF NIPFP ON EMPLOYMENT \n \n \n*6.   DR. KAMBHAMPATI HARIBABU: \n \n \nWill the Minister of LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether a Working Paper of the National Institute of Public Finance \nand Policy (NIPFP) has noted that laws relating to labour are at the \ncentre of anti-employment bias; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the reaction of the Government thereto; \n \n(c) whether the Government has taken any steps to ease the labour laws \nto generate more employment in the country; and \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE (IC) FOR LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n(SHRI BANDARU DATTATREYA) \n \n \n(a) to (d):  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n* \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) to (d) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *6 DUE FOR REPLY ON 17.07.2017 BY DR. \nKAMBHAMPATI HARIBABU, M.P. REGARDING “ WORKING PAPER ON NIP FP ON \nEMPLOYMENT” \n \n(a) to (d): According to the Working Paper on Employment, Education and the \nState, 2017 of the National Institute of Public Finance and Policy (NIPFP), there \nare several factors at work for the low growth of overall employment and the \nslow pace of transfer of workers from the unorganized to the organized sector \nresulting in a whole range of policies which collectively adds up to an anti -\nemployment bias.  \n \nGovernment has taken several steps for employment generation including \nreforms in labour laws as an ongoing process  to update legislative system to \naddress the need of the hour and to make them more effective and \ncontemporary to the emerging economic and industrial scenario.  \n \nThe Ministry has implemented the Shram Suvidha Portal that facilitates \ninspection of establis hments in a scientific and transparent manner. It also \nprovides for a common registration under Employees’ Provident Fund \nOrganisation (EPFO) and Employees’ State Insurance Corporation (ESIC) and \nfacilitates submission of monthly Electronic -Cum-Challan (EC R). The Ministry \nhas also rationalized the 56 register/  forms maintained under 9 Central labour \nlaws to 5 register/ forms. In addition for 3 labour laws applicable to both States \nand Centre the forms have been reduced from 36 to 12. These reforms will \nfacilitate compliance to labour laws. \n \nIn addition, a new Scheme “Pradhan Mantri Rojgar Protsahan Yojana” has been \ninitiated by the Ministry of Labour and Employment in the year 2016 -17 for \nincentivising industry for promoting employment generation with the a llocation \nof Rs. 1000 crore. Under this scheme employers would be provided an incentive \nto enhance employment where the Government will pay the employer’s \ncontribution of 8.33% EPS made to new employees. In textiles (apparel and \nmade-ups) sector, the Gover nment will also pay the 3.67% EPF contribution of \nemployers in addition to paying the 8.33% EPS contribution. Government has \nannounced a booster package of Rs 6000 crores for the textile sector which is \nan employment intensive sector. \n \nGovernment is also i mplementing the National Career Service having a portal \n(www.ncs.gov.in) for online registration and posting of jobs for job -seekers and \nprovide other employment related services. \n*****                                                            ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_60": "LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.60 \nFOR ANSWER ON 17/07/2017 \n \nFERRO SCRAP NIGAM LIMITED \n \n60. SHRI RAJESH VERMA: \n \nWill the Minister of STEEL be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is aware  of the anomalies in the performance  \nevaluation system of officers in various units of Ferro Scrap Nigam Limited (FSNL)  in \nthe country including the Burnpur Unit; and \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the corrective measures taken by the Government \nin this regard? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR STEEL         (SHRI VISHNU DEO SAI) \n \n(a)&(b): No, Madam. However, there have been some representations against the \ngrading awarded to one officer of the Burnpur  Unit of Ferro Scrap Nigam Limited \n(FSNL). The representations have been examined by FSNL and appropriate replies \ngiven to the concerned officer.  \n \n******** \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_61": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 61 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 17.07.2017 \n \nDIVERSION OF PF FUND INTO PMGPY \n61. MOHAMMED FAIZAL:  \nWill the Minister of LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT be pleased to \nstate:  \n(a)whether the Government has any plan to remit the share of \norganized sector labours Provident fund pension scheme to \nstrengthen the PMGPY Programme;  \n(b)if so, the details thereof;  \n(c)whether any representations/requests have been received in this \nregard; and  \n(d)if so, the details thereof along with the reaction of the Government \nthereto? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (IC) FOR LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n(SHRI BANDARU DATTATREYA) \n \n(a):  No such proposal is under consideration in the Ministry at \npresent.  \n(b):  Does not arise in view of reply to part (a) of the Question above.  \n(c):  No representations/requests in this regard have been received \nby Employees’ Provident Fund Organisation (EPFO).  \n(d):  Does not arise in view of reply of part (c) of the Question above. \n \n****** ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_62": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF WATER RESOURCES,\nRIVER DEVELOPMENT & GANGA REJUVENATION\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. †*62\nANSWERED ON 20.07.2017\nKEN-BETWA RIVER LINK PROJECT\n†*62. SHRI AJAY MISRA TENI\nWill the Minister of WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT AND GANGA\nREJUVENATION be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Government has started the work relating to inter -linking of Ken and Betwa rivers\nin the Bundelkhand region so that the region gets rid of drought and if so, the details thereof;\n(b) the details of the progress made in regard to the said project during the last three years;\n(c) the approximate hectare area of land turned barren due to lack of irrigation in Bundelkhand\nregion of Uttar Pradesh and Madhya Pradesh during the said period; and\n(d) the number of dams to be constructed by the Government in Bundelkhand region under the\nKen-Betwa river link project including the number of districts in which it is planned to provide\nirrigation facilities along with the time by which the said project is likely to be completed?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT AND\nGANGA REJUVENATION\n(DR. SANJEEV KUMAR BALYAN)\n(a) to (d) A statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n*****\n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) to (d) OF STARRED\nQUESTION NO. *62 TO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2017 REGARDING KEN -BETWA\nRIVER LINK PROJECT.\n(a) to  (d) The Hon’ble Supreme Court in the matter of Writ Petition (Civil) No. 512 of 2002 “In Re:\nNetworking of Rivers” along with Writ Petition (Civil) No. 668 of 2002 ordered that the Ken-Betwa\nRiver Link Project be taken up for implementation in the first instance.\nOn the basis of Memorandum of Understanding signed between the States of Madhya\nPradesh and Uttar Pradesh dated 25.8.2005, Detailed Project Reports (DPRs) of KBLP Phase-I & II\nhave been prepared and shared with the concerned States of Madhya Pradesh and Uttar Pradesh.\nThe Project has already received the following mandatory clearances:\n1. Techno-economic clearance has been accorded by the Advisory Committee on Irrigation,\nFlood Control & Multipurpose Projects of Ministry of Water Resources, RD & GR in its\nmeeting held on 8th July, 2016.\n2. The MoEF&CC issued wildlife clearance on 21st September, 2016.\n3. Expert Appraisal Committee (EAC) of MoEF&CC considered environment clearance in its\nfirst meeting held on 30 th December, 2016 and recommended the project for grant of\nenvironmental clearance.\n4. On the basis of recommendations of the Forest Advisory Committee (FAC), Central\nGovernment has granted the approval of Stage -I Forest Clearance for KBLP Phase -I vide\nMoEF&CC letter dated 25th May, 2017.\n5. Ministry of Tribal Affairs (MoTA) has examined the case and accorded the clearance vide\ntheir letter dated 4th January, 2017.\n6. The project proposal of KBLP has been recommended by the Investment C learance\nCommittee of the Ministry in its 5 th meeting held on 10th February, 2017 and the same has\nbeen considered acceptable for investment in the State Plan with an estimated cost of Rs.\n18057.08 crore at Price Level 2015-16.\nThe KBLP will provide irrigation to an area of 6,35,661 ha annually (3,69,881 ha in MP and\n2,65,780 ha in UP) in the Chhattarpur, Tikamgarh and Panna districts of Madhya Pradesh and\nMahoba, Banda, Lalitpur & Jhansi districts of Uttar Pradesh. In addition, the project will provide\n49 million cubic meter (MCM) of water for enroute drinking water supply to population of 13.42\nlakh of UP & MP.  The project will also generate 78 MW of power. The total construction period\nof the Project is about 8 years. A Draft Cabinet Note for implementation has been circulated on 30th\nMay, 2017 to concerned Ministries/Departments for their comments/views.\nThis Project was reviewed at a high level and it was decided that Ken -Betwa Link Project\n(KBLP) should be taken up for implementation through an SPV consisting of NHPC and\nContd…p/2\n\n//2//\nrepresentatives of Governments of Madhya Pradesh and Uttar Pradesh.\nThe status of the Project was further reviewed at a high level on 04.07.2017 with Chief\nSecretary, Govt. of Madhya Pradesh and Principal Secretary, Irrigation Department, Uttar Pradesh.\nThe Government of Madhya Pradesh has proposed that Kotha Barrage, Bina Complex and Lower\nOrr Dam be also included in the Project. Their status is as under:\nProject Status\nLower Orr DPR of lower Orr Dam submitted to CWC for appraisal on 4\nth\nJuly, 2017 – Under examination in CWC\nBina Complex\nDPR is under appraisal in CWC. The compliance to the CWC\nobservations is yet to be submitted by GoMP.\nKotha Barrage\nDPR of Kotha Barrage has been submitted to CWC for appraisal,\nin March, 2017 – Under examination in CWC.\nLeft  out areas in\nphase 1\nThe proposal is being prepared and will be submitted to CWC for\nappraisal by 31.7.2017.\nThis would also affect the initial allocation of water between the two States as per the 2005\nagreement.  It was therefore, decided that both the State Governments should work out an\nagreement on mutual water sharing to take KBLP forward. The implementation of KBLP would be\ntaken up once the two States have reached an agreement on water sharing.\nNo area of land turned barren due to lack of irrigation in Bundelkhand region of Uttar\nPradesh and Madhya Pradesh during period has been reported to the Ministry.\n*****",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_63": " \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 63 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 17th JULY, 2017 \n \nEXPANSION OF BHARAT-OMAN REFINERIES \n \n63: SHRI LAXMI NARAYAN YADAV: \n \nपैट्रो ल ियम और प्राकृ तिक गैस मंत्री \nWill the Minister of PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS be pleased to state: \n(a) whether any expansion work has been undertaken in the Bharat -Oman \nRefineries Limited during the last three years;  \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and  \n(c) the present status of the said expansion work? \n \nANSWER \nपैट्रोलियम और प्राक ृ लिक गैस मंत्रािय में राज्य मंत्री (स्विंत्र प्रभार) (श्री धमेन्द्र प्रधान) \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS (SHRI \nDHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n(a) to (c): BPCL has reported that Bharat -Oman Refineries Limited (BOR L) has \nundertaken a debottlenecking project to increase the refinery processing capacity \nfrom 6 to 7.8 Million Metric Tonne Per Annum (MMTPA) and also to meet the BS -VI \nproduct specifications. The estimated cost of the project is Rs. 3072 crores. The \nmechanical completion is scheduled for September 2018. As on June 15, 2017 \noverall cumulative physical progress of the project stands at 48%. \n \n \n************ ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_64": " \n \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 64 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2017 \n \nINSTALLATION OF SOLAR ROOFTOP SYSTEM \n \n*64. SHRI P.K.BIJU:   \n        SHRI KANWAR SINGH TANWAR:     \n                                                       \n Will the Minister of NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY be pleased to state: \n(a) the progress made in installati on of 4,200 MW solar rooftop system under the National \nSolar Mission with the budget of Rs.5000 crore allocated for the purpose in 2015;   \n     \n(b) whether the Government has kept any record of the numbers of houses in urban and rural \nareas which have rooftop solar panels supplying electricity and if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c) the measures taken by the Government to  increase the number of solar rooftop project s \nin residential areas of the country? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR POWER, COAL, NEW & RENEWABLE ENERGY AND \nMINES (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) (SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL) \n(a) to (c ): A statement is laid on the table of the House  \n******* \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \nStatement \nStatement referred to reply to Part (a) to (c) of Lok Sabha \nStared Question No.64 to be answered on 20.07.2017 \nPart (a): An aggregate capacity of 671 MWp grid connected rooftop solar \nsystems have been installed in the country so far. Out of this 283MWp is in \nindustrial segment, 175MWp  in commercial segment, 79MWp in institutional \nsegment, 29 MWp in domestic household segment, 101MWp in Government \nsegment and 4MWp in social sector segment   \nPart (b): 3727 houses have installed rooftop solar systems under the scheme \nPart (C): To increase number of solar roof top projects in residential sector, \nthe Government inter alia has taken following measures: \n Central Financial Assistance  on bench mark cost is offered  for individual \nhouse holds to the tune of 30% in G eneral Category States and to the tune of \n70 % in Special Category States(North East States, Himachal Pradesh, \nJammu and Kashmir, Uttarkhand, Andaman and Nicobar islands and \nLakshadweep islands)  \n  States have been motivated to bring out net -metering regulations for grid \nconnected rooftop solar power plants  and as on today  all 3 6 States/UTs \nStates/ UTs have notified such regulations and/or tariff orders. \n 1933 firms have been empaneled as Channel Partners for easy reference by \nthe households for execution of grid connected rooftop solar projects. \n   In addition to State Nodal Agencies, Solar Energy Corporation of India \n(SECI)    has  been executing   roof top solar projects in residential / social / \ninstitutional  sectors. \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_65": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF CULTURE\n \nLOK\n \nSABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. \n65\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON \n17\n.0\n7\n.201\n7\n \n \nSCHOLARSHIPS TO ARTISTS\n \n \n65\n: \n \n    \nSHRI RAVINDRA KUMAR PANDEY\n:\n \n           \n \n         \n \n \nWill the MINISTER OF CULTURE be pleased to state:\n \n(\na\n)\n \nwhether financ\nial help/scholarships are being provided to young artists for propagating, \nspreading and building their local culture in different parts of the country including \nJharkhand;\n \n \n(\nb\n)\n \nif so, the State\n-\nwise details of the States and artists who have been provided fun\nds during \nthe last two years; and;\n \n \n(\nc\n)\n \nthe steps taken/being taken by the Government to further motivate the artists?\n \n \nANSWER\n \nMINISTER OF STATE (IC) FOR CULTURE & TOURISM \n \n \n \n(DR. MAHESH SHARMA)\n \n \n(\na\n)\n \nYes, Madam. The Government is implementing Scheme of Scholarship\ns to Young \nArtistes in different cultural fields in different parts of the country including Jharkhand.\n \n \n \n(\nb\n)\n \nFor the batch year 2014\n-\n15, 212 Scholars were selected and for the batch year 2015\n-\n16, \n282 Scholars have been selected. State\n-\nwise details are annexed\n. Each selected artiste is \ngiven scholarship of Rs. 5000/\n-\n \nper month for a period of two years.\n \n \n(c)\n \nMinistry of Culture is administering various Schemes such as Cultural Talent Search \nScholarship Scheme (CTSSS), Fellowship Scheme, Cultural Function & Prod\nuction \nGrant Scheme (CFPGS) etc. for artists/outstanding persons in different fields of culture. \nIn addition to this Ministry of Culture provides financial assistance to its \nattached/subordinates offices and autonomous bodies for conducting various activit\nies \nsuch as Festivals, Seminars, Exhibitions through various Institutions under them to \nmotivate the artists.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n  \n\nAnnexure\n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (\nb\n)